## 4. Tauri Capability Permissions — Common Pitfall

Wrong permission names cause a **build failure** (not a runtime error). The build
script validates `capabilities/default.json` against the plugin manifest at compile
time. An unknown permission name exits 1 with a dump of all valid names.

Confirmed correct names for this project:

| Feature | Permission string |
|---------|-------------------|
| `relaunch()` JS (calls `plugin:process\|restart`) | `process:allow-restart` |
| File logging | `log:default`, `log:allow-log` |
| Save dialog | `dialog:allow-save` |
| Write file | `fs:allow-write-text-file` |

When adding a new plugin, run `check-dev.sh` immediately — the error message contains
the full valid permission list for that plugin.

---

## 5. Unit Tests

Run independently of `check-dev.sh` to check pure logic without starting the GUI:

```bash
# Rust — 22 tests: compute_blocked, sanitise_filename, type serialisation
cd desktop/src-tauri && cargo test

# Frontend — 30 tests: computeBlockedSections, sectionStatus, shortModel, escHtml,
#            statusLabel, validateManifestJson
cd desktop && npx vitest run
```

---

## 6. Frontend Error Flow

All JavaScript errors end up in the same `app.log` as Rust errors:

```
window.onerror / unhandledrejection
  → logError() in src/logger.ts
    → invoke('log_frontend_error', { context, message })
      → log::error!("[frontend::{}] ...", context, message)
        → ~/Library/Logs/com.editorllm.desktop/app.log
```

When debugging a frontend issue, read `app.log` first — it contains both Rust and
JS traces in chronological order.

---

## 7. Dev Server Lifecycle

| Command | Effect |
|---------|--------|
| `./check-dev.sh` | Kill old instance → start fresh → wait for result → exit |
| `npm run dev:log` | Start no-watch app, pipe output to `/tmp/editorllm-dev.log` |
| `npm run dev:static` | Start no-watch app, output to stdout only |
| `cat /tmp/editorllm-dev.pid \| xargs kill` | Kill the current dev server |

The PID of the running dev server is always in `/tmp/editorllm-dev.pid`.

---

## 8. Complete Verification Checklist

Before declaring any desktop-side task done:

- [ ] `./check-dev.sh` exits 0
- [ ] No `error` or `panicked` lines in `/tmp/editorllm-dev-clean.log`
- [ ] `cargo test` exits 0 (if any `.rs` files changed)
- [ ] `npx vitest run` exits 0 (if `src/utils.ts` or test files changed)
- [ ] Log shows `Finished` + `Listening on http://127.0.0.1:3847`
